  "query_preview": "..\n(Tomorrow through Monday)\nIssued at 1124 AM CDT Mon Oct 19 2026\n\nThe aforementioned wave moves into the plains on Tuesday, \nproviding more mid-high clouds and additional shower attempts, \nthough dry sub-cloud air should continue to severely limit any \nrainfall. Upper level ridging will dominate the forecast through \nthe remainder of the week, providing warming temperatures and dry \nconditions. Temps near or above 80 degrees are likely mid to late \nweek. Tightening MSLP gradients will tend to increase southerly \nwinds by late week, but should still remain less than 20 mph \noverall. Thus, while locally increased fire weather conditions \nwill be possible given low afternoon RHs, fire weather potential \ndoes not look overly concerning at this time. By this weekend and \ninto early next week, deterministic/ensemble guidance depicts \nanother trough moving into the plains, but with varying intensity.\nThis feature may push one or more cold fronts into the region \n(with increasing rain chances), but confidence remains low at this\ntime. Overall, the CPC continues to indicate above average \ntemperatures and near to above average precipitation are favored \nas we close out October.",
